## Symptom
The c2c skill (`SKILL.md` / using-c2c) does not make it obvious how to send to peers on another local repo broker via `--cross-repo`.

Agents reading the skill default to same-repo `c2c send <alias> <msg>` and miss the cross-repo sessions broker path (`c2c send --cross-repo …`, also `list` / `register` / `monitor` with `--cross-repo`). Discovery and addressing for machine-local, other-repo peers is easy to overlook.

## Expected
- Skill core flow (send / discover / list) explicitly documents `--cross-repo` (and `C2C_SESSIONS_BROKER_ROOT` override) as the way to reach peers registered on the machine sessions broker rather than this repo's broker.
- Short example: `c2c list --cross-repo` then `c2c send --cross-repo <alias> <msg>`.
- Clarify that bare `<alias>` without `--cross-repo` is same-repo only; cross-host remains `<alias>@<host_id>` via relay (distinct concern).

## Acceptance
- [ ] Skill tables / habits mention `--cross-repo` next to send/list/register/monitor.
- [ ] At least one concrete CLI example for cross-repo DM.
- [ ] Distinguishes same-repo / same-host (`--cross-repo`) / relay (`alias@host`) in one short note.

## Discovery
Operator request 2026-07-23: skill should make cross-repo messaging more obvious.